## Exact algebraic preflight

For the hybrid shell (2), pairwise cancellation gives

```text
(1/2) sum_n v_n n^T = F
```

for all symbolic `F`, fronts, and outcomes.  If outcome `a` is replaced by
outcome `b` while the five live cells are transported unchanged, defining

```text
F' = F + (r_(f,a)-r_(f,b)) f^T/2
```

gives exactly

```text
2 F' f + r_(f,b) = 2 F f + r_(f,a),
F' n = F n for n perpendicular to f.
```

Thus no live quantum state needs copying, resetting, or outcome-dependent
rewriting.  The physical five-cell packet can remain unchanged while its
decoded matrix updates telescopically with the newest Record.

## Generated-front geometry preflight

After a Record forms at `x`, the five edges

```text
x+f       -> x+2f,
x+/-e_1   -> x+f+/-e_1,
x+/-e_2   -> x+f+/-e_2
```

are pairwise disjoint nearest-neighbor edges.  Their SWAPs clear the next
target `x+f` and place the five live contents at exactly its forward and
lateral neighbors.  The new Record at `x` is its backward neighbor.

The newest Record content selects `x+f`.  Every older Record points forward
to a site that already has a Record, so the no-overwrite rule leaves exactly
one unrecorded selected site along the generated straight front.  This is a
prospective induction witness; the registered runner must enumerate two-step
local neighborhoods and prove the general prefix invariant.

